| MOS component                  | Language                       | Why                                                        |
| ------------------------------ | ------------------------------ | ---------------------------------------------------------- |
| PostgreSQL / schema            | **SQL**                        | Database is the source of truth                            |
| Core daemon / node runtime     | **Rust**                       | Memory safety + excellent performance                      |
| Network protocol               | **Rust**                       | Strong typing, async, safe concurrency                     |
| Workers                        | **Rust + Python**              | Rust for production workers, Python for ML/experimentation |
| LLM/ML inference               | **Python**                     | Best ecosystem                                             |
| Embedding pipeline             | **Python / Rust**              | Python initially; Rust for optimized production paths      |
| Retrieval engine               | **Rust**                       | Very performance-sensitive                                 |
| Graph algorithms               | **Rust**                       | Excellent for CPU-heavy traversal/algorithms               |
| API server                     | **Rust**                       | Safe, fast, async                                          |
| SDK                            | **TypeScript + Python + Rust** | Covers most agent ecosystems                               |
| CLI                            | **Rust**                       | Single portable binary                                     |
| Dashboard                      | **TypeScript**                 | React/Svelte/etc.                                          |
| Migration tooling              | **SQL + Rust**                 | SQL migrations controlled by Rust CLI                      |
| Testing                        | **Rust + Python + SQL**        | Different layers need different testing                    |
| Performance-critical utilities | **Odin or Rust**               | Odin is viable here                                        |


The Rust runtime would provide things like:

Event ingestion
Memory operations
Provenance enforcement
Versioning
Worker scheduling
Network communication
Authentication
Authorization
Retrieval orchestration
Caching
Resource management
Observability

The database remains authoritative.

Rust becomes the safe execution layer around it.
